<title>GERMANY: German June trade surplus falls to 7 bln marks.</title>
<headline>German June trade surplus falls to 7 bln marks.</headline>
<dateline>WIESBADEN, Germany 1996-09-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Statistics Office reported the following economic indicator (bln marks):</p>
<p> GERMAN TRADE/CURRENT ACC  June 96   May 96    June 95</p>
<p> Trade balance		 +7.0     +9.5(+9.5)    +8.8</p>
<p> Current account	     -2.1     -2.5(-2.5)    +0.7</p>
<p> Exports			 60.9     62.8(62.8)    63.9</p>
<p> Imports			 53.9     53.3(53.3)    55.1</p>
<p> Services			-4.3     -4.9(-4.9)    -6.0</p>
<p> Wage and property income  +0.9     -1.8(-1.8)    +2.6</p>
<p> Transfers		     -5.3     -4.9(-4.9)    -4.2</p>
<p> Supplementary trade	 -0.4     -0.4(-0.4)    -0.5</p>
<p>GERMAN TRADE/CURRENT ACC  Jan-June 96	Jan-June 95</p>
<p> Trade balance		  +45.5	     +44.5</p>
<p> Current account		 -8.8		-4.1</p>
<p> Exports			  371.1	     362.8</p>
<p> Imports			  325.6	     318.3</p>
<p> Services			 -24.2	     -26.1</p>
<p> Wage and property income    -1.5		+4.2</p>
<p> Transfers			-26.9	     -25.4</p>
<p> Supplementary trade	   -1.7		-1.3</p>
<p>-- Bonn newsroom, 49 228 26097150</p>
